  "decision": "A unique historical clone is not ruled out solely by its directory name, but exact original UUID recovery is unproven. Do not spend the native lane on a reconstruction presented as reliable recovery.",
  "findings": [
    "Pinned upstream LLD hashes the entire pre-strip linked buffer plus final output basename, before code-signature hashing. Absolute output directory is not separately seeded.",
    "Participating debug-map object/archive absolute paths and source compilation directories can change those bytes. Later stripping does not recalculate the UUID.",
    "Current Chromium ThinLTO driver creates a random temporary saved-object directory. Participating debug-bearing LTO objects can therefore change debug-map path bytes even on a same-root fresh link. This is a source mechanism, not a performed two-build comparison.",
    "External app resources and separate dSYM paths are not automatic framework UUID inputs; they matter only through bytes or identifiers actually linked into the framework."
  ],
  "requiredGate": "Full original framework and dSYM UUID equality remains necessary before original framework symbolization. Never force a UUID or use approximate current offsets.",
